Finding 1 (must fix, small): a refused start gives a reply with no reason or a stale one.
- Where: supervisor.go:583-586 and :593-596 return without setting lastErr. handle (:729-731) then answers with snapshot(): Running false, Desired true, LastError "".
- What the user sees: serviceAction (cmd/launcher/tools.go:236-237, startFailure :245-247) and the console's act (cmd/launcher/lifecycle.go:365-366) turn that into: Error: service "ue" did not start: (nothing after the colon).
- The MCP server stays up until wg.Wait() returns (main.go:415-418), so ue_start and ue_restart can reach this window.
- If an earlier start failed and the backoff is pending, the reply shows that old error instead, which is misleading.
- My probe confirmed the reply: {Running:false Desired:true LastError: LastExit:}.
- Before k182 the reply said running, and the editor was then killed. k126 made this reply say why a start failed. This change gives it an empty reason.
- Suggested fix: set lastErr (e.g. "shutting down") on both refused paths, and assert r.st.LastError in TestControlCallTakenAtTheShutdownStartsNothing (cancel_test.go:319). Nothing else reads lastErr, because the loop ends on the next turn.

Confirmed, no finding:
- Next turn after a refused start: backoff is nil, cmd is nil, and nothing re-arms the timer, so the loop can see only ctx.Done() and waiting calls. Each waiting call is answered without a start. With finitely many callers the loop ends; it cannot hang. A call that arrives after the loop has ended runs into the 10 s ctrlTimeout ("not responding"). That was already so in v0.0.9 and is not part of this card.
- Desired flag: a refused ctrlStart or ctrlRestart leaves desired=true and clears restarts, quickFails and lastExit. No one reads any of them after shutdown. The reply says "desired, not running", which matches what the call asked for. ctrlRestart's stop() still kills the process, and the shutdown would have killed it anyway.
- k37/k179 stop rule: unchanged. A stop never goes through start(). The stop peeks at :759-761 and :808-809 and the main select are untouched.
- Path (a), the main select picking a waiting call over ctx.Done(): covered. Once Done is closed, ctx.Err() is non-nil, so start() refuses. My probe: exitTaken queues a status and then a start in a buffered ctrl (cap 2) and cancels. The peek takes the status, so the main select sees ctx.Done() and the start together. Tree: 50/50 pass; in 23 of them the main select took the start and refused it. Overlay without both checks: 26/50 fail (PreStart [false false]). A probabilistic check is all that path allows, which agrees with the worker's "no seam" note.
- PreStart failing during shutdown: PreStart is func(Start) and cannot report a failure. editorPreStart drops kill and remove errors and logs no WARN. The refused path returns before c.Start, countRun, giveUp and startFailed, so there is no "start failed" WARN, no fast-fail count, no OnExit and no give-up line. Only "[<name>] not started: shutting down" is logged.
- German: none in the touched text.

